#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:1
msgid "Overlapping Transfers and Compute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:3
msgid ""
"Pageable host memory is convenient, but CUDA may stage it through internal "
"page-locked memory before a DMA transfer. That extra staging work limits "
"asynchronous copies. `PinnedHostBuffer<T>` gives CUDA a stable host address "
"for direct transfer. True copy/compute overlap also requires asynchronous "
"copies on non-default streams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:9
msgid "Run the complete demo with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:11
msgid "cargo oxide run pinned_overlap\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:15
msgid ""
"The example uses a cheap in-place increment kernel, so its timing is "
"dominated by data movement rather than computation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:18
msgid "Choosing a copy API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:20
msgid ""
"The safe helper synchronizes the stream before returning. Use it when the "
"host does not need to do other work while the copy is in flight:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:23
msgid ""
"device.copy_to_pinned_host(&stream, &mut host)?;\n"
"// `host` is safe to read because the helper synchronized `stream`.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:28
msgid ""
"The async helper returns before the copy finishes. The caller owns the "
"synchronization and the buffer lifetime:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:31
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: `host` and `device` stay alive and are not reused until `done` "
"fires.\n"
"unsafe { device.copy_to_pinned_host_async(&stream, &mut host)? };\n"
"let done = stream.record_event(None)?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:37
msgid ""
"The caller must keep both buffers alive, must not read or mutate an in-"
"flight host buffer, and must wait for the stream work before dropping or "
"reusing it. The same rule applies to `copy_from_pinned_host_async`. Pre-"
"allocate device buffers and refill them; `from_pinned_host` still performs a "
"synchronous device allocation before enqueuing its copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:43
msgid "Rotating pinned staging buffers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:45
msgid ""
"Operations stay ordered within one stream, while independent streams can "
"make progress concurrently on hardware that supports concurrent copy and "
"compute:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:48
msgid ""
"stream 0: upload 0 -> kernel 0 -> download 0 -> upload 3 -> kernel 3\n"
"stream 1: upload 1 -> kernel 1 -> download 1 -> upload 4 -> kernel 4\n"
"stream 2: upload 2 -> kernel 2 -> download 2 -> upload 5 -> kernel 5\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:54
msgid ""
"The example gives each stream a persistent `DeviceBuffer`, a pinned staging "
"buffer, and a completion event. Upload, kernel, and download are already "
"ordered by the stream, so the event is only needed to protect host-side slot "
"reuse. Before reusing a slot, the host waits for its event, copies out the "
"completed result, and then refills the staging buffer. The final stream join "
"drains all work before CUDA-owned memory is dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:61
msgid ""
"The core enqueue sequence inside the example's loop is shown below; "
"surrounding setup and result handling are omitted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:64
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: the slot buffers stay alive and are not reused until completion.\n"
"unsafe {\n"
"    devices[slot].copy_from_pinned_host_async(&streams[slot], "
"&stagers[slot])?;\n"
"    module.increment(&streams[slot], config, &mut devices[slot])?;\n"
"    devices[slot].copy_to_pinned_host_async(&streams[slot], &mut "
"stagers[slot])?;\n"
"}\n"
"completions[slot] = Some(streams[slot].record_event(None)?);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:74
msgid ""
"The complete setup, slot-reuse wait, and final drain are in the "
"[`run_overlapped` implementation](https://github.com/NVlabs/cuda-oxide/blob/"
"main/crates/rustc-codegen-cuda/examples/pinned_overlap/src/main.rs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:77
msgid "Measured impact"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../async-programming/overlapping-transfers-and-compute.md:79
msgid ""
"The bandwidth benchmark warms up three times, records ten CUDA-event "
"samples, and reports their median. The pipeline benchmark measures host wall "
"time for eight 32 MiB chunks. The serialized path allocates and synchronizes "
"a pageable device buffer for each chunk. The overlapped path pre-allocates "
"three device buffers and pinned staging buffers, then includes host staging "
"copies, event waits, and result copies in its wall time. The result is "
"therefore an end-to-end path comparison, not a pure copy-engine measurement."
msgstr ""

